---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';

const title = 'GraceLock - Terms of Use';
const description = 'Terms of Use for GraceLock - Pray & Screen Time';
---

<Base head={{ title, description }}>
	<Section>
		<article class="prose prose-gray dark:prose-invert max-w-4xl mx-auto">
			<h1>Terms of Use for GraceLock</h1>
			<p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Last updated: November 25, 2026</p>

			<p>
				These terms apply to <strong>GraceLock - Pray &amp; Screen Time</strong> ("GraceLock", "the app"), published by <strong>tskulbru</strong>. By using the app you agree to them. If you downloaded GraceLock from the App Store, Apple's <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Standard EULA</a> also applies.
			</p>

			<h2>Using GraceLock</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>GraceLock helps you pray before opening apps you choose to block. Blocking depends on permissions you grant (Screen Time on iOS, the Accessibility service or Usage Access on Android) and on your device keeping GraceLock running. If you turn those off, or your device stops the app, blocking stops.</li>
				<li>GraceLock is a tool for building a habit, not a parental control or security product. Don't rely on it to keep anyone away from content.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>GraceLock Premium</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Premium is an auto-renewing subscription (weekly or yearly). Prices are shown in the app before you buy.</li>
				<li>Payment is charged to your Google Play or Apple account. The subscription renews automatically at the same price unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the end of the current period.</li>
				<li>If a free trial is offered, you are charged when the trial ends unless you cancel before then.</li>
				<li>Cancel anytime in Google Play (Payments &amp; subscriptions) or in your Apple ID subscription settings. Refunds are handled by Google or Apple under their policies.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Content</h2>
			<p>
				Prayers and Bible verses are provided for devotional use.
			</p>

			<h2>No warranty and limitation of liability</h2>
			<p>
				GraceLock is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind. To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses arising from your use of the app. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under consumer protection law.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				We may update these terms; the date above shows the latest version. You can stop using GraceLock at any time by deleting the app.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>Questions? Email <a href="mailto:gracelock@tskulbru.dev">gracelock@tskulbru.dev</a>.</p>

			<div class="mt-12 p-6 bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg">
				<p class="text-sm text-center text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
					<a href="/" class="hover:text-orange-600 transition-colors">&larr; Back to tskulbru.dev</a> |
					<a href="/apps/gracelock-privacy" class="hover:text-orange-600 transition-colors">Privacy</a> |
					<a href="/apps/gracelock-support" class="hover:text-orange-600 transition-colors">Support</a>
				</p>
			</div>
		</article>
	</Section>
</Base>
